    <innerclass refid="classscl_1_1feature_1_1inplace_1_1plain" prot="public">scl::feature::inplace::plain</innerclass>
    <innerclass refid="classscl_1_1feature_1_1inplace_1_1uninitialized" prot="public">scl::feature::inplace::uninitialized</innerclass>
    <briefdescription>
<para>Built-in executor strategies for <computeroutput>scl::wrapper</computeroutput>. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>An executor is a class template that controls how the wrapper stores the held value and dispatches method calls to it. Each executor must provide two static member function templates:</para>
<para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><computeroutput>execute(self, func, args...)</computeroutput> — runs <computeroutput>func</computeroutput> with <computeroutput>args</computeroutput> and returns its result; may add cross-cutting behaviour around the call.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>value(self)</computeroutput> — returns a reference to the held value, propagating the cv-ref qualifiers of <computeroutput>self</computeroutput>.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><table rows="3" cols="3"><row>
<entry thead="yes"><para>Executor   </para>
</entry><entry thead="yes"><para>Storage   </para>
</entry><entry thead="yes"><para>Overhead    </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput><ref refid="classscl_1_1feature_1_1inplace_1_1plain" kindref="compound">scl::feature::inplace::plain</ref></computeroutput>   </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>in-place, direct   </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>none    </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput><ref refid="classscl_1_1feature_1_1inplace_1_1uninitialized" kindref="compound">scl::feature::inplace::uninitialized</ref></computeroutput>   </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>in-place, raw aligned storage   </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>none   </para>
</entry></row>
</table>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
